413 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The analysis reveals that TV marketing investment does not consistently translate into higher GMV or order volume for luxury products, highlighting inefficiencies in spend allocation. While some months see a strong correlation between investment and returns, others \(e.g., month 8\) show disproportionate spending with minimal impact, signaling potential wastage. To maximize ROI, a strategic shift toward high-performing digital and premium-targeted marketing channels is crucial for luxury product success.)
/E (The analysis reveals that TV marketing investment does not consistently translate into higher GMV or order volume for luxury products, highlighting inefficiencies in spend allocation. While some months see a strong correlation between investment and returns, others \(e.g., month 8\) show disproportionate spending with minimal impact, signaling potential wastage. To maximize ROI, a strategic shift toward high-performing digital and premium-targeted marketing channels is crucial for luxury product success.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
